  "status": "ACTIVE_CANDIDATE_POLICY",
  "goal": "Preserve regression memory while keeping canonical Ordo language conformance, Vibe authoring policy, Auto Answers test-scenario policy, and runtime-adapter compatibility as separate authority layers.",
  "principles": [
    "Regression memory is domain-neutral: business-specific dogfood defects are reduced to minimal generic fixtures.",
    "Factory-owned validators are authoritative for shared contracts; a generated package-local validator may add domain checks but cannot replace or weaken trusted factory gates.",
    "A candidate with any machine-detectable failure is repaired internally and is not presented to the analyst as a usable alpha.",
    "The successful live dogfood revision is a positive control; regression hardening must not reject a proven-good runtime shape.",
    "Ordo-valid but Editor-unsupported constructs are classified as Editor gaps, not silently prohibited as language defects.",
    "Canonical Ordo language is the sole semantic source of truth; runtime adapters cannot redefine language validity.",
    "Auto Answers defects are repaired in the test scenario unless the playbook itself violates Ordo.",
    "Adapter incompatibility is reported distinctly from Ordo invalidity.",
    "A corrected runtime adapter replaces obsolete workarounds in adapter contracts; historical adapter bugs remain regression tests rather than playbook constraints."
  ],
